From: OHOS Dev <dev@ohos.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0114] Fix test_time.test_monotonic_settime SIGSYS crash on OHOS

test_monotonic_settime calls clock_settime(CLOCK_REALTIME) to jump the system
clock backward by 1 hour then restore it. On OHOS, clock_settime triggers
SIGSYS (signal 31) because the kernel's seccomp filter returns a signal
instead of EPERM, killing the entire test process.

test_clock_settime already has this skip (added in earlier patches), but
test_monotonic_settime was missed. This patch adds the missing skip.

---
 Lib/test/test_time.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Lib/test/test_time.py b/Lib/test/test_time.py
index abcdef..1234567 100644
--- a/Lib/test/test_time.py
+++ b/Lib/test/test_time.py
@@ -598,6 +598,7 @@ class TimeTestCase(unittest.TestCase):
         self.assertGreaterEqual(t2, t1)
 
     @unittest.skipUnless(hasattr(time, 'clock_settime'),
+    @unittest.skipIf(sys.platform == 'ohos',
+                     "clock_settime() triggers SIGSYS on OHOS "
+                     "(kernel returns signal instead of EPERM)")
                          'need time.clock_settime')
     def test_monotonic_settime(self):
         t1 = time.monotonic()

